From 24078866166aab2f28e7043ca33054973fc19920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:54:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Model ICU mutex ownership for strict Clang analysis

Annotate ICU mutexes, C wrappers, and scoped guards without disabling thread-safety analysis. Identify the global default guard explicitly, release the currency cache mutex on allocation failure, and use standard conditional lock ownership in the transliterator.

TDD: bazel test //third_party/v8:icu_mutex_analysis_test fails against the original ICU headers at held-on-return and unheld-release diagnostics (icu-bazel-red.log, exit 1). The final patched test passes, including both ICU libraries (icu-bazel-unique-lock.log, exit 0). The negative target fails specifically for both unprotected guarded writes (icu-negative-analysis.log, exit 1). Materialized ICU files match all five authoring inputs byte for byte. just fmt-check passes (icu-format-final.log).

Base: rust-v0.162.1, 092d3acd6bec3e3a14bdc7e7a2810ab628ab759d. Verification prerequisites: current toolchain and native warning policy patches. Fixes holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed#61 in the ICU scope.
